        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ollama): models advertise tools when /api/show fails",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users discovering local Ollama models would still see tool support advertised when `/api/show` failed (HTTP error or network throw), so a broken or uninspectable model looked tool-capable in catalog/setup paths.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\n`buildOllamaModelDefinition` treats missing `capabilities` as optimistic `supportsTools: true`. Failed `/api/show` previously returned `{}`, which left capabilities undefined. This change returns empty `capabilities` on show failure, matching the existing setup inspect contract, while leaving a successful show that omits capabilities optimistic.\n\n## User Impact\n\nLocal Ollama models whose `/api/show` fails no longer advertise tools. Models that never got a show response still keep the previous optimistic tools default. Empty-capability failures stay uncached so a later successful show can retry.\n\n## Evidence\n\n| Layer | Proof | Result |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| L1 | `provider-models.test.ts` HTTP 404 / throw → `supportsTools: false`; oversized show → `{ capabilities: [] }` | pass |\n| L2 | `buildOllamaProvider` enrich → definition on mocked tags/show fail | pass |\n| L3 | Real `127.0.0.1` HTTP (`/api/tags` 200, `/api/show` 500) + undici `fetch` (no `vi.stubGlobal`) | pass |\n\nScrapable L3 line:\n\n```text\n[ollama show-fail live proof] base=http://127.0.0.1:53733 model=stale:latest showHits=1 supportsTools=false\n```\n\nLocal gates on touched files:\n\n```text\npnpm exec oxfmt --check extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.ts extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.test.ts\npnpm exec oxlint extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.ts extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.test.ts\npnpm exec vitest run extensions/ollama/src/provider-models.test.ts\n→ 24 passed\n```\n\nHead: `b6928f41a6a5464c9568bcf29c5ceb742a34492a`  \nCompare: 2 files, ~+122/−3\n\nMade with [Cursor](https://cursor.com)",
